  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-23 (independent auditor, after a59427f8c0). RFC 8654 Section 3: \"Peers that wish to use the BGP Extended Message Capability MUST support error handling for BGP UPDATE messages per [RFC7606].\" The only change to a tagged unit is a comment in TestRFC7606MPReachNLRIConsistentWithAFISAFIAccepted (validateMPReachAttr renamed validateMPNLRIField); its body, an IPv4 MP_REACH whose /8 ends flush with the attribute giving exact ActionNone through ValidateUpdateRFC7606, is unchanged and ran green. The extended-message session units in rfc_receive_session_dispatch_test.go and rfc8654_rib_recovery_test.go are unchanged and still prove the RFC 7606 actions (attribute discard, treat-as-withdraw with route removal, duplicate MP reset) apply on a session with extended messages. Verdict stands. Findings recorded outside this verdict: that unit's doc comment still says \"Untagged\" though it carries the RFC8654-3-1 positive tag, and the discrimination records on the rfc_receive_session_dispatch and rfc8654_rib_recovery units no longer verify (producer-changed applyRFC7606).",
